sam: Heads-up: we've had a few support tickets where customers ship `undici` into browser/edge bundles because the SDK imports it at module top-level. That increases bundle size and breaks edge workers. We should stop top-level imports.

rachel: +1. Solution: lazy/dynamic import only when needed. If globalThis.fetch exists, use it. Otherwise do a dynamic import('undici') at runtime. That keeps bundlers from statically pulling it in.

tyler: Also make `undici` optional (peer or optionalDependency) so install isn't forced. Document `npm i undici` as an opt-in for Node <18.

nisha: Small TS gotcha: many projects omit "dom" from tsconfig libs and then get missing Fetch/Headers types. Add a troubleshooting snippet in quickstart.

sam: Example helper (keeps ESM + CJS in mind):
```ts
// packages/sdk/src/runtime/fetch-detect.ts
export async function getRuntimeFetch(): Promise<typeof fetch> {
  if ((globalThis as any).fetch) return globalThis.fetch;
  try {
    const undici = await import('undici');
    return (undici as any).fetch;
  } catch (e) {
    try {
      // CJS fallback for older node setups
      // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-var-requires
      const req = require('undici');
      return req.fetch;
    } catch (e2) {
      throw new Error('No fetch available. Install undici or run on a runtime with fetch.');
    }
  }
}
```

rachel: Docs should show how to pass a custom fetch to the client too (clientOptions.fetch) and mention why you'd do that (custom tracing, special headers).

tyler: Runtime matrix to add to CI: Node 18, Node 20, Next.js server, Next.js edge, Vercel Edge, Cloudflare, Bun (experimental). Add sanity checks that the SDK bundle doesn't include undici when building for edge.

nisha: TS snippet for docs:
```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["es2021", "dom"],
    "target": "es2021"
  }
}
```

sam: Another runtime quirk: AbortController/AbortSignal semantics vary. We should add a small helper and guidance: create a fresh AbortSignal per request, don't reuse signals across retries. Maybe expose `makeAbortController()` in the SDK utils.

rachel: We should also mention stream differences: server-side streaming on Node vs web-workers can behave differently; call out that we don't guarantee byte-for-byte identical stream implementations across runtimes.

tyler: Packaging note: keep conditional exports so CJS users still get require entry and ESM users get import entry. Also ensure `types` points to dist/types/index.d.ts so TS tooling works.

ci-bot: CI run 2483: packaging + smoke tests on Node 18/20 passed. Edge bundle size check: undici not present in edge builds.

sam: Action items: (1) add runtime fetch detector helper and use internally (no top-level undici imports), (2) make undici optional and document install path, (3) update sample apps (next-server, next-edge, simple-node) with tsconfig examples, (4) add CI runtime matrix and bundle-size check. I'll open the PR and tag reviewers.

nisha: I'll add the tsconfig troubleshooting paragraph and a tiny note about @types/undici if people install it.

rachel: I'll prepare the sample-app diffs and the README blurb.

sam: Thanks folks. If you see other edge cases (Deno, quickstart for monorepos), drop them in the PR discussion. :rocket:
